The development of this software makes use of a number of excellent third-party open source libraries. We would like to express our sincere gratitude to the contributors of these projects. Below is the list of third-party code libraries that this software currently uses or has used in the past, together with their license information.

License: SPDX identifier of the license under which the component is used.
Copyright: quoted verbatim from the license file shipped with the component. Where the license text contains no copyright line, this is stated explicitly.
Usage: how the component is used on the dev branch.
  - vcpkg: fetched by vcpkg at build time; its source is not included in this repository.
  - Bundled source: the source code is kept in this repository under Inkeys/additional/.
  - Git submodule: included as a Git submodule.
  - Distributed with the program: embedded in the program as a binary.
  - No longer used: no longer compiled or linked on the dev branch; kept here for the historical record.

This list is a summary only. The license text of each component prevails.

